You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Laptop Opening Mockup (`mockup-laptop-open`)

A laptop that opens as it scrolls into view: the lid hinges up from closed in 3D, the screen wakes with a flash of glow, then the content fades in.

## What it should do
Build a laptop-open mockup with Motion: a lid (aspect 16:10 bezel + screen) with transform-origin bottom animating rotateX −88° → 0 over 1.4 s when in view (perspective on the parent), a base with a notch below; after the lid opens, flash a white overlay (0 → .35 → 0) and fade the content from bright to normal.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/mockup-laptop-open.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Screen content is real HTML; reduced motion shows it open immediately.
- **Performance:** One rotateX transform and two opacity fades, once.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

